  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">La Paz Water Efficiency &amp; Early Warning Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The larger La Paz Water Efficiency &amp; Early Warning Project is subdivided into two sub-projects:- Sub-project A; Reduction of Non-revenue water and Early warning system, and- Sub-project B; Rehabilitation and expansion of the Pampahasi water treatment plant.The overall objective of the larger project is to ensure a permanent, sufficient and good quality supply of water by an organization (EPSAS) that is able to fully cope with the increasing demand for water and that supplies the necessary trust for water related private sector development. Sub-Project B entails the rehabilitation and expansion of the treatment capacity of the Pampahasi Plant from 700 l/sec to 1200 l/sec.</narrative>
  </description>
